transactions, which

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:05.070
can be easily avoided by using
a hybrid approach of machine

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.240
learning and a
rule-based approach.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.590
47 of these frauds
which are happening--

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.060
these credit card frauds--

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.850
are actually happening
in the United States.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:18.300
And every retailer-- on
the average, the retailers

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.580
are dealing with, per month,
approximately 442 fraud

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.660
attempts.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.320
There is a financial loss.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.749
The loss is not just because
of the credit card loss--

00:02:30.749 --> 00:02:32.040
the frauds which are happening.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.080
It's the operation loss too.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.120
A lot of manpower
is required to go

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.620
through each and
every transaction,

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:43.040
monitor them, and reduce
the false positives.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.240
What are the trends related
to data compromises?

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:49.630
There are four categories
I have bucketed.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:55.690
The first one is frequency,
magnitude, sophistication,

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.270
and organization.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.920
What does this mean?

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.550
If I go with the frequency
and magnitude first,

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:08.020
it means the frauds are
happening very frequently

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.660
with a large impact.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:15.190
As I said, the impact is not the
money loss between these frauds

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.300
when it is happening.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.280
It's the operation loss.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:21.910
The current system, there is
a high false positive rate.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.260
Because of this
high false positive,

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.500
there is a manpower
which is required

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.640
to go through each
and every alert

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.600
which the system has generated.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.590
So that's the reason the
frequency and the magnitude

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.330
are the worst, I would
say, enemies of the data

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.780
compromises.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.810
The next one is sophistication.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.060
The fraudsters are
much more smarter.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.450
They know how to tackle
that rule-based approach.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.250
What they are doing
is they are coming up

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:54.180
with new and different ways
of committing these frauds.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:56.040
The algorithms
what they are using

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.510
are very sophisticated--
very difficult to catch.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.010
And because of that, what we
require in our existing fraud

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.070
system, they should be
able to customize based

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.710
on these new emerging trends.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:14.430
But what is happening,
the way these solutions

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:17.649
are integrated there is
the making of customization

00:04:17.649 --> 00:04:22.950
to that adds a lot of delay
in the time to market.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:26.340
That's where the Capgemini has
partnered with Google Cloud

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:30.440
Platform to come up with a
solution which actually make

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:37.080
easy way of doing customization
and reduce the time to market.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.420
The last one is organization.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.490
The frauds are not just
limited to external.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.040
The frauds are not
limited to what

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.720
may be happening on the
terminals, ATM, branches.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.720
There is lot of internal
fraud which is happening,

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:55.330
the internal fraud done
by the internal staff,

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.640
in the internal processes,
and on the internal terminals.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.670
So that is what we call
as an insider threat.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.960
So these are the four main
buckets where the data

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.728
compromises are happening.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.180
Now what is CPP?

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.920
For today's session,
we are mainly

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.770
focused on the common
point of purchase.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:22.500
The solution we
have built is around

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.260
how this, on the
various terminals,

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.240
the compromise is happening.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.760
So what is that?

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:34.890
It means when the fraudster
is using the skimming devices

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:39.120
on the cash machines or
the point-of-sale devices

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.060
to collect information
about the cards.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.030
You are going to Wal-Mart,
you are going to Target--

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:49.960
there might be some machine
where the fraudsters have put

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:51.880
this type of a skimming device.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:54.610
You are swiping your
cards, and your information

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:56.980
is getting collected.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:01.000
That particular terminal becomes
the common point of purchase,

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.740
and when you see
there is a trend

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:04.930
happening that a
lot of customers

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:08.140
are complaining
on having a fraud.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:11.860
And most of them are swiping on
that particular terminal, that

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:15.670
is what we call as to
uncover the CPP, which

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:20.870
is required to uncover the
fraud which is happening.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:22.280
How we can handle that?

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:26.010
By analyzing the transactional
data at a regular basis.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.920
A CPP algorithm can collect
a lot of information-- a lot

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.830
of insights.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:38.840
Tracing, for instance, tracing
where these cards are getting

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:39.440
swiped.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.370
What is the geolocation?

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:45.740
The demographic information
about the customers.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:51.320
Identifying all the terminals
where this fraud is happening.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:57.880
And providing a list of at-risk
cards so the detection is--

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.020
OK, if the fraud
has happened, we

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:02.075
know that these are the
10 cards or 20 cards

00:07:02.075 --> 00:07:05.750
or hundreds of cards which
are getting compromised.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.450
But how we can do
the prevention?

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:11.900
How we can identify
proactively which are

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.900
the cards which are at risk?

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:19.280
Our existing solutions are
more rule-based approach.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.350
When a customer
complains or there

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:25.190
is an anomaly in the
transaction, it sends an alert.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.010
But sometimes because,
as they are rule-based,

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.790
the false positives
is very high.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:34.270
Finding exactly the
terminal-- finding

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:37.330
it more proactive,
more faster, is not

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:38.740
possible in the
existing systems.

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:45.280
Now what can be done when
this type of frauds happen?

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:48.740
One is sending the right
alert to the merchant,

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.490
that at this
particular terminal,

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:56.140
there is a skimming device that
customers' card information are

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.060
getting compromised.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:00.950
The second one is that a
way the banks are handling

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:04.310
is, they change the cards.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.260
But it's a very
expensive affair.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.750
Changing the card, sending
the new cards to the customers

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:13.840
is very, very expensive
to the organization.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.380
That's why it is very
important that not only be

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:19.170
reactive in fraud
analytics, but it also

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:22.540
be very important to
be proactive in finding

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:25.320
where this compromise
is getting happen.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:28.050
Now about our solution.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:31.560
As I said, we have partnered
with Google Cloud Platform.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:36.150
We have come up with a
comprehensive solution that

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:41.010
is helping our client detect,
prevent, and analyze fraud

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:44.550
by using a hybrid approach--
machine learning along

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:46.680
with a rule-based approach.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:48.840
Now how we have
come up with that?

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.000
As Capgemini
Financial Services, we

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.290
have multiple banking customers
from both issuing side

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.000
and acquiring side.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.080
We did the whole assessment.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.960
What is the current scenario?

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.060
What are the current
gaps in the system--

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.400
fraud solutions?

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:08.080
What is the business need?

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:12.900
And after talking to a lot
of folks in these banks,

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.170
we have come up with a
different business needs.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:20.040
What the solution currently
exists, and what are the gaps

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:23.730
and how we can fill by building
a new solution on Google Cloud

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:24.230
Platform.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.930
So to begin with, what
is a business need?

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:35.170
First, everyone wants to
reduce false positive.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.240
There is lot of noise in
a rule-based approach.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.410
Because of this noise, the
false positives increase.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.660
And there is a whole
lot of team which

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:49.340
is sitting, going manually
each and every transaction,

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:51.560
and figuring out
whether it's really

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.580
a fraud or a false positive.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:58.540
So first, everyone wants to
reduce the false positive.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:02.670
Second, detect the fraud
faster, before it impacted

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:05.560
the huge customer base.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.520
As I said, by the time
the fraud happened,

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.480
they wait for the
complaint or any anomaly,

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:14.650
the fraudsters start using
and selling in the dark web

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:17.200
all the card information.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.090
And large number of
customers are getting

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:22.550
impacted because of that.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:26.940
The next one is moving the fraud
system to cloud environment.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:30.770
If you wanted to make the
detection more faster, more

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.620
quicker, and using
a machine learning,

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:36.770
it's important to have more
cloud environment instead

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:40.370
of the on-prem environment.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.590
The next one is
flexible pricing model.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:45.620
This is one of our
key differentiators

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.140
of our solution.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:51.690
The existing solutions are
very, very tightly coupled.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:53.600
If you wanted to
have a menu card

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:56.390
of where the customers
can pick and choose

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:57.830
based on their need--

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:02.110
that I need these components--
maybe network and analysis,

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:07.550
Customer 360, anomaly
detection, or insider threat.

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:10.880
That type of a facility is
not available in the existing

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:12.380
solution.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.910
They are so coupled.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:17.520
Because of that, they
are very expensive.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:21.050
What we have created is we
have created a menu card which

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.120
we are giving to our customers.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.570
They pick and choose
based on your need.

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:29.090
Don't change your
existing ecosystem.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:32.120
Don't change your
existing architecture.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.720
Pick up these accelerators, make
it part of your architecture,

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.090
and make it more smarter.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:42.620
So that reduce
the time to market

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:45.410
and make the
decisions more faster.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:47.839
And that's the beauty of cloud
environment and especially

00:11:47.839 --> 00:11:48.755
Google Cloud Platform.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:53.640
The next one is automation.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:56.800
As I said, going through each
transaction, a lot of manpower

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:57.300
is required.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:03.730
There is a department which goes
through each and every alert.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:05.460
How we can automate the process?

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:09.990
How we can highlight or send
the right alerts to the end

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:13.500
customers, and the right
folks in the banks?

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.256
So the automation--
the workflows

00:12:15.256 --> 00:12:17.005
are very, very important
in this solution.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.350
The next is enhancing
the customer

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:25.730
behavior profiles and
uncover hidden relationships.

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:28.280
When we talk about the
customer, and especially

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.470
if you have to figure
out the location where

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:34.310
these terminals exist,
it's very important

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:37.460
to use the third-party
information of geolocation.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:41.620
So we have partnered with some
data providers who give us

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:46.040
a zip code plus four information
so that we can drill down--

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:49.780
exactly pinpoint
where, which terminal,

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:52.590
this fraud is happening.

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:56.070
And not only that, we have
integrated our Customer 360

00:12:56.070 --> 00:13:00.300
solution in it, where we create
a holistic view of the customer

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:04.830
to understand how they
are swiping these cards.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:07.220
Because it gives us
information that, OK,

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:10.650
if this terminal at
this particular retailer

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:13.020
has compromise,
there is a chance

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:16.710
that next 50 customers
are going to swipe there,

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:17.820
because that's a trend.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:20.520
That's about a Customer 360.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.760
So creating that whole
transaction information,

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:27.840
their personal information--
creating one, more than an MDM,

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:33.730
that's what we create a holistic
view of the end customers.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:36.030
So these are the
six business needs

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:38.640
which get highlighted
by our financial service

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:40.380
organizations.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:46.220
And based on that, we come up
with our fraud analytics CPP

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.290
solution.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:53.460
Now in this CPP solution,
we have five components.

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:59.090
First, how to do fraud
detection faster.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:03.250
Find the fraud
transaction by location.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:07.420
As I said, we are drilling
down into zip code plus four,

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:11.470
figuring out where exactly
it is happening so that we

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:15.640
can create a zone and find
that who all customers are

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.580
more likely to swipe
in next five days.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:24.940
That is where our system is of
a solution is more proactive

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:30.010
and helps the organization
in taking decisions faster.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:32.600
Next is network analysis.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:35.380
So this is a very
nice component,

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:38.000
which Jules is
going to demo, where

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.010
we create a complete network
analysis of the retailers

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:44.830
and the customers.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:49.210
This is visually able to
help the teams in the bank

00:14:49.210 --> 00:14:52.000
to figure out who are
the next customers who

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.650
are going to in that.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:55.670
If customers are
